+ '<p class="l-text">Quantization replaces 32-bit floating point weights with 8-bit integers. This reduces model size by ~4x, speeds up CPU inference by 2-4x (modern CPUs have hardware INT8 pipelines), and fits larger batches into memory — with minimal accuracy loss (typically &lt;1% F1).</p>'

