+ '<div class="calc-step"><div class="step-num">2</div><div class="step-body"><strong>Get soft labels</strong> — Run the teacher on training data and record the full softmax output (probability distribution over classes), not just the argmax. These "soft labels" carry richer information than 0/1 hard targets.</div></div>'
+ '<div class="calc-step"><div class="step-num">3</div><div class="step-body"><strong>Define distillation loss</strong> — Train the student with a combined loss: <code>L = α·CE(student, hard_labels) + (1-α)·KL(student_soft, teacher_soft)</code>. The KL divergence term forces the student to match the teacher\'s uncertainty, not just its predictions.</div></div>'
+ '<div class="calc-step"><div class="step-num">4</div><div class="step-body"><strong>Train the student</strong> — The student architecture is smaller (fewer layers, smaller hidden size). It learns from both ground truth and the teacher signal simultaneously.</div></div>'
+ '<div class="calc-step"><div class="step-num">5</div><div class="step-body"><strong>Deploy the student</strong> — The teacher is discarded. The student is deployed. It serves faster and cheaper while preserving most of the teacher\'s accuracy. Apply quantization on top for further gains.</div></div>'
