+ '<div class="calc-highlight">'
+ '<strong>Why PEFT?</strong> Full fine-tuning updates every weight in the model. BERT-base has 110 million parameters. BERT-large has 340 million. GPT-3 has 175 billion. At FP32, that\'s 700 GB just to store the gradients for GPT-3 — before optimizer states. Full fine-tuning is impossible at scale. PEFT methods freeze the base model and train only a tiny fraction of parameters, achieving comparable results at a fraction of the cost.'
