/* ── 1a. ONNX Export ─────────────────────────────────────── */
+ '<h4 style="color:#c8a96e;margin:24px 0 10px">1.1 — ONNX Dışa Aktarımı</h4>'
+ '<p class="l-text">ONNX (Open Neural Network Exchange), eğitimi (PyTorch) çıkarımdan (herhangi bir ONNX uyumlu runtime) ayıran standartlaşmış bir model formatıdır. ONNX Runtime (ORT), Microsoft\'un optimize edilmiş çıkarım motorudur — grafik optimizasyonlarını, kernel füzyonunu ve donanıma özgü hızlandırmayı otomatik olarak uygular.</p>'

+ '<div class="code-wrap"><div class="code-label"><span>PYTHON (DEMO)</span> ONNX Export &amp; ORT Inference <button class="code-copy">COPY</button></div><div class="code-block"><pre><code>'
+ '<span class="cm"># Step 1: Export your fine-tuned model to ONNX</span>\n'
+ '<span class="kw">import</span> torch\n'
+ '<span class="kw">from</span> transformers <span class="kw">import</span> AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForSequenceClassification\n\n'
+ '<span class="cm"># Load your trained model</span>\n'
+ 'model_path = <span class="str">"./sentiment-bert-finetuned"</span>\n'
+ 'tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.<span class="fn">from_pretrained</span>(model_path)\n'
+ 'model = AutoModelForSequenceClassification.<span class="fn">from_pretrained</span>(model_path)\n'
+ 'model.<span class="fn">eval</span>()\n\n'
+ '<span class="cm"># Create dummy input (BERT expects input_ids, attention_mask)</span>\n'
+ 'dummy_input = <span class="fn">tokenizer</span>(\n'
+ '    <span class="str">"This is a sample sentence for tracing."</span>,\n'
+ '    return_tensors=<span class="str">"pt"</span>,\n'
+ '    max_length=<span class="num">128</span>,\n'
+ '    padding=<span class="str">"max_length"</span>,\n'
+ '    truncation=<span class="kw">True</span>\n'
+ ')\n\n'
+ '<span class="cm"># Export to ONNX</span>\n'
+ 'torch.onnx.<span class="fn">export</span>(\n'
+ '    model,\n'
+ '    args=(dummy_input[<span class="str">"input_ids"</span>], dummy_input[<span class="str">"attention_mask"</span>]),\n'
+ '    f=<span class="str">"sentiment_bert.onnx"</span>,\n'
+ '    input_names=[<span class="str">"input_ids"</span>, <span class="str">"attention_mask"</span>],\n'
+ '    output_names=[<span class="str">"logits"</span>],\n'
+ '    dynamic_axes={\n'
+ '        <span class="str">"input_ids"</span>:      {<span class="num">0</span>: <span class="str">"batch_size"</span>, <span class="num">1</span>: <span class="str">"seq_len"</span>},\n'
+ '        <span class="str">"attention_mask"</span>: {<span class="num">0</span>: <span class="str">"batch_size"</span>, <span class="num">1</span>: <span class="str">"seq_len"</span>},\n'
+ '        <span class="str">"logits"</span>:         {<span class="num">0</span>: <span class="str">"batch_size"</span>}\n'
+ '    },\n'
+ '    opset_version=<span class="num">13</span>,\n'
+ '    do_constant_folding=<span class="kw">True</span>  <span class="cm"># fuse constant subgraphs</span>\n'
+ ')\n'
+ '<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="str">"ONNX export complete: sentiment_bert.onnx"</span>)\n\n'
+ '<span class="cm"># Step 2: Run inference with ONNX Runtime</span>\n'
+ '<span class="kw">import</span> onnxruntime <span class="kw">as</span> ort\n'
+ '<span class="kw">import</span> numpy <span class="kw">as</span> np\n\n'
+ 'session = ort.<span class="fn">InferenceSession</span>(\n'
+ '    <span class="str">"sentiment_bert.onnx"</span>,\n'
+ '    providers=[<span class="str">"CUDAExecutionProvider"</span>, <span class="str">"CPUExecutionProvider"</span>]\n'
+ ')\n\n'
+ '<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">ort_predict</span>(text: <span class="fn">str</span>) -> <span class="fn">dict</span>:\n'
+ '    inputs = <span class="fn">tokenizer</span>(\n'
+ '        text, return_tensors=<span class="str">"np"</span>, max_length=<span class="num">128</span>,\n'
+ '        padding=<span class="str">"max_length"</span>, truncation=<span class="kw">True</span>\n'
+ '    )\n'
+ '    logits = session.<span class="fn">run</span>(\n'
+ '        [<span class="str">"logits"</span>],\n'
+ '        {<span class="str">"input_ids"</span>: inputs[<span class="str">"input_ids"</span>],\n'
+ '         <span class="str">"attention_mask"</span>: inputs[<span class="str">"attention_mask"</span>]}\n'
+ '    )[<span class="num">0</span>]\n'
+ '    probs = np.<span class="fn">exp</span>(logits) / np.<span class="fn">exp</span>(logits).<span class="fn">sum</span>(axis=-<span class="num">1</span>, keepdims=<span class="kw">True</span>)\n'
+ '    label = <span class="str">"POSITIVE"</span> <span class="kw">if</span> probs[<span class="num">0</span>][<span class="num">1</span>] > <span class="num">0.5</span> <span class="kw">else</span> <span class="str">"NEGATIVE"</span>\n'
+ '    <span class="kw">return</span> {<span class="str">"label"</span>: label, <span class="str">"confidence"</span>: <span class="fn">float</span>(probs[<span class="num">0</span>].<span class="fn">max</span>())}\n\n'
+ '<span class="cm"># Benchmark</span>\n'
+ '<span class="kw">import</span> time\n'
+ 'text = <span class="str">"The film was absolutely brilliant and deeply moving."</span>\n'
+ 'N = <span class="num">100</span>\n'
+ 'start = time.<span class="fn">time</span>()\n'
+ '<span class="kw">for</span> _ <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="fn">range</span>(N): <span class="fn">ort_predict</span>(text)\n'
+ '<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="str">f"ORT avg latency: {(time.time()-start)/N*1000:.1f}ms"</span>)\n'
+ '<span class="cm"># Typical result: ~12ms vs ~45ms for PyTorch CPU</span>'
+ '</code></pre></div></div>'
+ '<p class="l-text"><strong>ONNX dışa aktarımı + ORT çıkarım akışı nasıl çalışıyor:</strong> 1) <code>torch.onnx.export(model, args=(dummy_input["input_ids"], dummy_input["attention_mask"]), f="sentiment_bert.onnx", input_names=[...], output_names=["logits"], dynamic_axes={...}, opset_version=13, do_constant_folding=True)</code> PyTorch grafiğini bir dummy input ile izler ve taşınabilir bir ONNX dosyası üretir; <code>dynamic_axes</code> batch boyutu ve dizi uzunluğunun çalışma zamanında değişmesine izin verir. 2) <code>ort.InferenceSession("sentiment_bert.onnx", providers=["CUDAExecutionProvider", "CPUExecutionProvider"])</code> ONNX grafiğini mevcut en iyi yürütme arka uçuyla yükler. 3) <code>ort_predict(text)</code> numpy\'ye tokenize eder, <code>session.run(["logits"], {...})</code> çağırır, softmax uygular ve <code>{"label": ..., "confidence": ...}</code> döndürür. 4) 100 yinelemeli benchmark ORT\'yi (~12 ms) PyTorch CPU (~45 ms) ile karşılaştırır — bedavaya yaklaşık 4× hızlanma.</p>'

/* ── 1b. Quantization ────────────────────────────────────── */
+ '<h4 style="color:#c8a96e;margin:24px 0 10px">1.2 — Quantization: FP32 → INT8</h4>'
+ '<p class="l-text">Quantization, 32-bit kayan noktalı ağırlıkları 8-bit tam sayılarla değiştirir. Bu, model boyutunu ~4 kat azaltır, CPU çıkarımını 2-4 kat hızlandırır (modern CPU\'ların donanım INT8 pipeline\'ları vardır) ve daha büyük toplu işlemlerin belleğe sığmasını sağlar — minimal doğruluk kaybıyla (genellikle &lt;%1 F1).</p>'

+ '<div class="code-wrap"><div class="code-label"><span>PYTHON (DEMO)</span> Dynamic &amp; Static Quantization <button class="code-copy">COPY</button></div><div class="code-block"><pre><code>'
+ '<span class="cm"># Dynamic quantization — fastest to apply, no calibration data needed</span>\n'
+ '<span class="kw">import</span> torch\n'
+ '<span class="kw">from</span> torch.quantization <span class="kw">import</span> quantize_dynamic\n\n'
+ 'model_fp32 = AutoModelForSequenceClassification.<span class="fn">from_pretrained</span>(model_path)\n\n'
+ 'model_int8 = <span class="fn">quantize_dynamic</span>(\n'
+ '    model_fp32,\n'
+ '    {torch.nn.Linear},               <span class="cm"># quantize Linear layers only (positional arg)</span>\n'
+ '    dtype=torch.qint8\n'
+ ')\n\n'
+ '<span class="cm"># Compare sizes</span>\n'
+ '<span class="kw">import</span> os\n'
+ 'torch.<span class="fn">save</span>(model_fp32.<span class="fn">state_dict</span>(), <span class="str">"/tmp/bert_fp32.pt"</span>)\n'
+ 'torch.<span class="fn">save</span>(model_int8.<span class="fn">state_dict</span>(), <span class="str">"/tmp/bert_int8.pt"</span>)\n\n'
+ 'fp32_mb = os.path.<span class="fn">getsize</span>(<span class="str">"/tmp/bert_fp32.pt"</span>) / <span class="num">1e6</span>\n'
+ 'int8_mb = os.path.<span class="fn">getsize</span>(<span class="str">"/tmp/bert_int8.pt"</span>) / <span class="num">1e6</span>\n'
+ '<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="str">f"FP32: {fp32_mb:.0f} MB  |  INT8: {int8_mb:.0f} MB  |  Reduction: {fp32_mb/int8_mb:.1f}x"</span>)\n'
+ '<span class="cm"># Typical: FP32: 418 MB  |  INT8: 106 MB  |  Reduction: 3.9x</span>\n\n'
+ '<span class="cm"># Static quantization (better accuracy, needs calibration)</span>\n'
+ '<span class="kw">from</span> optimum.onnxruntime <span class="kw">import</span> ORTQuantizer, AutoQuantizationConfig\n\n'
+ 'quantizer = ORTQuantizer.<span class="fn">from_pretrained</span>(model_path)\n'
+ 'qconfig = AutoQuantizationConfig.<span class="fn">avx512</span>(is_static=<span class="kw">False</span>, per_channel=<span class="kw">False</span>)  <span class="cm"># production CPU; arm64() ARM\'da</span>\n'
+ 'quantizer.<span class="fn">quantize</span>(save_dir=<span class="str">"./bert-quantized"</span>, quantization_config=qconfig)\n'
+ '<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="str">"Quantized model saved to ./bert-quantized"</span>)'
+ '</code></pre></div></div>'
+ '<p class="l-text"><strong>İki quantization yolu nasıl karşılaştırılır:</strong> 1) <strong>Dinamik quantization:</strong> <code>quantize_dynamic(model_fp32, {torch.nn.Linear}, dtype=torch.qint8)</code> her <code>nn.Linear</code>\'i anlık olarak INT8\'e yeniden yazar — kalibrasyon verisi gerekmez ama yalnızca Linear katmanlar dönüştürülür. 2) <code>torch.save</code> + <code>os.path.getsize</code> bloğu etkiyi ölçer: ~418 MB FP32 vs ~106 MB INT8, 3.9× azalma. 3) <strong>Statik ONNX quantization:</strong> <code>ORTQuantizer.from_pretrained(model_path)</code> + <code>AutoQuantizationConfig.avx512(is_static=False, per_channel=False)</code> + <code>quantizer.quantize(save_dir="./bert-quantized", quantization_config=qconfig)</code> modeli üretim x86 CPU\'ları için donanım ayarlı INT8 kernelleriyle ONNX Runtime üzerinden dışa aktarır (modern Intel/AMD\'de <code>avx512()</code>, ARM sunucularda <code>arm64()</code> kullanın).</p>'

/* ── calc-compare: FP32 vs FP16 vs INT8 ─────────────────── */
+ '<div class="calc-compare">'
